From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: arm64: dts: qcom: add Xiaomi Piano board resources

Describe the Piano board, integrate the needed SM8750 nodes and keep the model in the DT build list.

The port retains changes from these linux-piano commits:
piano: bringup: integrate display and touch for first-light testing (bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>)
piano: dts: enable the peach WLAN/BT combo (PCIe0 + uart14 + PMU) (bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>)
piano: dts: bring up ADSP/CDSP remoteprocs and the audioreach audio chain (bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>)
piano: dts: correct qcom,msm-id for ABL hardware matching (bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>)
piano: NT36532 THP touch bring-up (milestone-touch) (#11) (bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>)
piano: native display (NT36532 DSC) and Adreno 830 GPU (#14) (bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>)
piano: FS19xx speakers on LPAIF TDM and the q6v5 handover IRQ fixes (bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>)

Co-authored-by: bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>

Link: https://github.com/blu-sharky/linux-piano/commit/cdac406e8b060769d9c5366e823217493fe6dbee
Link: https://github.com/blu-sharky/linux-piano/commit/0d1a34cf63ebb5fc6cd2ffc29fb2a1ca5a058deb
Link: https://github.com/blu-sharky/linux-piano/commit/54a5028967c34cd99d1583e1d751926c743bdf6c
Link: https://github.com/blu-sharky/linux-piano/commit/d43afa75440721478a94349b44a04108fa6692d8
Link: https://github.com/blu-sharky/linux-piano/commit/00b055cd9c1634371cd501530ba5c29de4ab91d4
Link: https://github.com/blu-sharky/linux-piano/commit/5c2c95fddbe9c29720b7b4e84119357358e9f0cb
Link: https://github.com/blu-sharky/linux-piano/commit/2f6c29345edf991b04ce15d2231e6060412335aa
Link: https://github.com/slwyts/Project-SunUEFI/commit/e8fcf33971263f28085dbc0dbe5039438bf76c13

Use the mainline SM8750 GPU, GMU, power, and cooling nodes. The
Piano port adds its board description and the REGDMA register
range used by its display pipeline.
